# GitHub push targets

Owner: **izoo2003** · email **izaanmujeeb420@gmail.com** · repo **Kafi-Sales-Agent**.

When the user asks to push, commit-and-push, sync, or “ship it” to GitHub:

- Push to **both** remotes (same branch, typically `main`):
  1. `origin` → `https://github.com/izoo2003/Kafi-Sales-Agent.git`
  2. `kafi-group` → `https://github.com/kafi-group/Kafi-Sales-Agent.git`
- Use: `git push origin HEAD` then `git push kafi-group HEAD` (or the branch’s existing upstream on each remote).
- No PR unless asked. Do not push to other remotes unless the user explicitly asks.
- The `vercel` remote (`izoo2003/kafi_sales_agent`) is separate — do **not** push there unless the user explicitly asks.
- If unsure which remote is which, run `git remote -v` before pushing.
- Do not change `git config` user.name / user.email unless the user explicitly asks.
